{"id": "EUVD-2026-104302", "enisaUuid": "2929f311-cd98-3bd3-a9d2-472bb4abe64a", "description": "libdisplay-info through 0.4.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the DisplayID v1 section parser in displayid.c that occurs when a data block's declared length exceeds the section. Attackers can supply a crafted EDID from a malicious monitor, KVM, capture device, or EDID file to make is_all_zeroes read past the buffer, causing a possible crash.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T14:11:35", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/libdisplay-info-displayid-datablock-overrun-oob-read", "https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/emersion/libdisplay-info/-/blob/0.4.0/displayid.c#L603-L689", "https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/emersion/libdisplay-info", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libdisplay-info-through-0.4.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-displayid-v1-parser"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112271", "GHSA-3gg9-cc9m-vj8c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c2fb9f37-1b50-39ce-b6cb-a71696055df7", "product": {"name": "libdisplay-info", "vendor": {"name": "emersion"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.4.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d2e66ed1-2cb7-365a-8a75-10e2b767091e", "vendor": {"name": "emersion"}}], "isExploited": false}